  unitName: Berserk Ezra
  unitId: 860978
  unitNumber: 8649
  description: An awakened Ancient is not to be trifled with, even if she bears the
    vessel of a young girl.Once, the Morokai and the Deva were one. Known as the
    Ancients, they were possessed of incredible power, but the first apocalypse sundered
    their souls in twain. Long had the powerful Morokai overlord Azurai sought a
    means to seize this power for himself through the Ritual of Awakening, but it
    would first require the blood of an awakened Ancient. Thus did he set his sights
    on young Ezra, born of Morokai and Deva blood. With the assistance of High Inquisitor
    Aranvis, a trap was laid and sprung, and Ezra fell within their dark grasp.The
    Rih'alnase, free-spirited Morokai warriors under the banner of their chieftain
    Avani, tore a bloody path of rescue toward their young charge alongside her adoptive
    uncle, the Deva librarian Allanon. By the skin of their teeth and nearly at the
    cost of Allanon's life, the dark ritual was reversed, but a glimpse of the half-awakened
    Ancient within Ezra was a nightmare for the ages.Had the intrepid band failed
    in their mission, Ezra would have most certainly lost her mind from the influx
    of uncontrollable power. The awakened Ancient would have then gone on to wreak
    havoc across all of Eneroth, leaving naught but a trail of destruction in her
    wake, and not even the famed overlord Azurai could hope to stop her. All that
    would remain of their war-torn world would be ash and blood. For their sakes,
    and perhaps especially for that of the Rih'alnase and Allanon, it was just as
    well such a fate had not come to pass. Yet such possibilities still resurface
    in the dark depths of one's mind while walking the straits of traumatic memory...
  summonDesc: Rrraagghh...!
  fusionDesc: Grrr...Grrrrr....
  evoDesc: GRRRAAAGGHHH!!!
